WEBVTT

00:05.297 --> 00:07.841
[Bechir, on radio] Rescue station one.
This is Sheriff Clemmons.

00:07.925 --> 00:10.761
All available fire and rescue
to Patricia's Cocktails.

00:10.844 --> 00:12.638
I don't know what the fuck is going on!

00:13.138 --> 00:15.140
[pensive music playing]

00:39.873 --> 00:42.876
[chattering]

00:48.173 --> 00:51.176
[chattering continues]

01:05.315 --> 01:07.025
[sighs] Every time.

01:30.966 --> 01:32.259
[fly buzzes]

01:39.057 --> 01:41.268
[ominous music playing]

01:49.943 --> 01:52.196
[chattering, laughing]

01:52.279 --> 01:54.364
["Blue" playing on speakers]

01:58.035 --> 01:59.286
[host chuckles]

02:00.412 --> 02:01.455
Patricia.

02:03.290 --> 02:05.375
You said I should stop by?

02:06.001 --> 02:09.545
Of course. Yeah, of course, come on in.

02:20.098 --> 02:21.099
[chuckles]

02:27.356 --> 02:28.982
Um, should I open this bottle?

02:29.691 --> 02:33.278
Yeah. We're all drinking white,
but if you want to, feel free.

02:34.446 --> 02:36.281
- Cool.
- [host] Just in the kitchen.

02:41.995 --> 02:43.997
[chattering]

02:47.751 --> 02:51.171
[guest 1] He snores when he's laying on
his back. He snores when he's on his side.

02:51.255 --> 02:53.423
I swear to God,
if he doesn't stop snoring, I'm just…

02:53.507 --> 02:55.425
I'm gonna smother him
with a pillow. [laughs]

02:55.509 --> 02:58.637
My dad snored so loud my mom
made him sleep on the couch,

02:58.720 --> 03:00.180
and you could still hear him…

03:00.264 --> 03:02.724
- My ex was the worst snorer.
- …all the way up--

03:02.808 --> 03:05.602
- And I'm telling you, it was the worst.
- Um…

03:05.686 --> 03:07.771
Not just the smell,
and it smelled pretty bad…

03:09.356 --> 03:11.358
[speaking indistinctly]

03:13.610 --> 03:15.320
[chuckles]

03:16.196 --> 03:17.906
[host] Oh, please don't open that.

03:18.490 --> 03:21.952
- Oh, um… Here. Here it is.
- Um…

03:24.371 --> 03:27.249
- I think it's clean. [chuckles]
- [chuckles] Thank you.

03:27.332 --> 03:29.168
- [groans]
- I don't think we've met. [chuckles]

03:29.251 --> 03:33.505
Um, I just moved here a few months ago
from Portsmouth. I'm Shelby.

03:33.589 --> 03:35.174
- Patricia.
- Hi.

03:36.925 --> 03:40.679
[groans] Lenore's
the only person I know here,

03:40.762 --> 03:44.057
hence the reason
I'm already on my third glass of wine.

03:44.141 --> 03:45.684
- [huffs]
- [chuckles]

03:45.767 --> 03:47.186
What about you? Who do you know?

03:47.269 --> 03:50.480
Um. Oh, I, uh, um,
graduated with most of them,

03:50.564 --> 03:51.815
but I'm usually pretty busy,

03:51.899 --> 03:54.067
so I don't often make it to these things.

03:55.736 --> 03:57.362
Can I ask you about it?

03:59.072 --> 04:00.073
What?

04:00.866 --> 04:02.784
The girls that died here.

04:02.868 --> 04:05.621
You… You must have all
gone to school together.

04:06.663 --> 04:07.831
Did I know them?

04:07.915 --> 04:08.916
[Shelby] Yeah.

04:10.501 --> 04:11.835
I was almost one of them.

04:13.795 --> 04:15.214
No.

04:15.714 --> 04:16.882
Yeah.

04:16.964 --> 04:18.926
And what happened? I'm sor… [scoffs]

04:19.009 --> 04:21.428
I shouldn't be asking you that.
I mean, it must be so hard to talk about.

04:21.512 --> 04:23.430
Um, it started with the calls… [stammers]

04:23.514 --> 04:27.726
…weird breathing and hang-ups,
and then one night I was alone.

04:27.809 --> 04:30.979
Oh, my God. Did he come to your house?

04:31.063 --> 04:32.439
The Boogeyman?

04:33.106 --> 04:34.775
Holy shit.

04:35.567 --> 04:38.779
Um, I heard someone downstairs
and I just knew--

04:38.862 --> 04:41.323
- Your gut instinct.
- Yeah. Exa… That's right.

04:41.406 --> 04:43.408
And I just thought, is this when I--

04:43.492 --> 04:44.618
- Whoa!
- Excuse me.

04:44.701 --> 04:47.329
- [guest 2] Oh, I'm sorry.
- Oh, no. Oh, it's fine.

04:47.412 --> 04:50.415
Oh, no, I…
It looks like she-she really got ya.

04:50.499 --> 04:51.917
- Oh, yeah.
- [Shelby chuckles] Shoot.

04:52.000 --> 04:53.418
All right, well… [chuckles]

04:53.502 --> 04:55.963
I'm gonna run to the bathroom
real-real quick, but then, um,

04:56.046 --> 04:58.173
- I have questions for you.
- Yeah, okay.

04:58.257 --> 04:59.591
- [chuckles]
- [chuckles] Yeah.

05:08.350 --> 05:09.351
Okay.

05:10.519 --> 05:12.104
["Morning" playing on speakers]

05:12.187 --> 05:15.482
[guest 1] We've all heard it a few times.
I mean, how many times can you lie?

05:15.566 --> 05:17.401
[guest 3] You know,
they even checked the phone records

05:17.484 --> 05:19.862
- and they proved she never got the calls.
- [guest 4] That's right.

05:19.945 --> 05:21.947
[guest 3] Twenty-five years
she's been telling that story.

05:22.030 --> 05:24.741
[host] She'll tell anyone who will listen.
It's honestly so pathetic.

05:24.825 --> 05:26.994
- [guest 3] Crazy.
- [host] She's, like, on another level.

05:27.077 --> 05:28.871
- I know.
- She is certifiable.

05:28.954 --> 05:30.956
- [host chuckles] You're so right, Kris.
- She's nuts. Yes.

05:31.039 --> 05:32.332
[host] It was the first thing she did

05:32.416 --> 05:34.126
- when she got here.
- [Kris clears throat]

05:34.877 --> 05:35.878
[host] Hmm.

05:39.089 --> 05:40.215
[smacks lips]

05:40.299 --> 05:42.593
Um, do you think you could
grab a picture of us?

05:42.676 --> 05:44.845
- [guest 2] Oh.
- Yeah. Sure.

05:46.513 --> 05:47.848
- Great.
- [host] All right.

05:47.931 --> 05:49.766
Come on, ladies. Everybody get together.

05:49.850 --> 05:51.059
Yeah. Back there. Come on.

05:51.143 --> 05:52.394
Get my best side. [chuckles]

05:52.477 --> 05:54.146
- All my friends together.
- Oh, yes.

05:54.813 --> 05:55.981
Say wine and cheese.

05:58.025 --> 06:00.235
- There we go.
- [guests cheer, chuckle]

06:00.861 --> 06:03.155
- Well…
- [host] You see, we only have, like, two.

06:03.238 --> 06:04.364
- I know.
- That's a good one.

06:04.448 --> 06:05.449
- Later on.
- Later.

06:05.532 --> 06:07.534
[crickets chirping]

06:20.506 --> 06:22.132
[door opens]

06:33.435 --> 06:35.437
[eerie music plays]

07:03.465 --> 07:05.634
[inhales deeply, sighs]

07:33.203 --> 07:36.456
[Patricia whispering]
"What don't you love about yourself?"

07:38.208 --> 07:41.086
I care too much

07:41.170 --> 07:46.717
what other people think.

07:56.143 --> 07:57.144
Hmm.

08:01.940 --> 08:03.358
[sighs]

08:10.365 --> 08:14.453
"Feeling like you could die tomorrow
and no one would notice?

08:14.536 --> 08:16.413
Well, that could be.

08:17.164 --> 08:20.209
But the right party can change that."

08:20.792 --> 08:22.461
[hopeful music playing]

08:22.544 --> 08:26.548
"The perfect hostess exudes confidence,

08:27.382 --> 08:29.134
effortless and elegant."

08:30.552 --> 08:31.637
"Elegant."

08:38.769 --> 08:43.190
"Suddenly, everyone knows you
as someone who throws great parties.

08:44.650 --> 08:48.862
All it takes is one
to change people's minds.

08:49.821 --> 08:53.158
All it takes is one great party
to change your life."

09:05.420 --> 09:07.297
Rosemary, here are the supplies.

09:07.381 --> 09:10.759
And Dale, you're gonna need a turntable
'cause you're gonna DJ.

09:10.843 --> 09:12.970
[chuckles] I've never done that before.

09:13.053 --> 09:14.429
Oh, you're gonna have them all dancing.

09:14.513 --> 09:16.723
There won't be a single moment of silence.

09:16.807 --> 09:19.226
Each song will blend
seamlessly to the next.

09:19.309 --> 09:22.521
Everyone's gonna talk about that night
they danced at Sunset Cocktails

09:22.604 --> 09:24.523
and that is all gonna be down to you.

09:25.649 --> 09:27.526
Okay, maybe you should hire someone.

09:27.609 --> 09:28.819
[Patricia] You'll be fine.

09:29.945 --> 09:30.946
[stammers]

09:31.029 --> 09:32.823
[pensive music playing]

09:32.906 --> 09:33.907
[exhales deeply]

09:43.500 --> 09:44.501
[sighs]

09:49.381 --> 09:52.384
[breathes deeply]

09:53.302 --> 09:54.303
[sighs]

09:58.599 --> 10:01.852
[hopeful music playing]

10:26.752 --> 10:29.963
Okay, so we're gonna put
the floral arrangements up here.

10:30.047 --> 10:32.049
I want that to be
the first thing people see,

10:32.132 --> 10:35.552
and we're gonna need to move some tables
out of here for the dance floor,

10:35.636 --> 10:37.346
or do you think
that'll make it look too big?

10:38.055 --> 10:39.056
I don't know.

10:39.139 --> 10:41.391
Okay. Well, um, what's next?

10:41.475 --> 10:44.478
I got catering,
which I'm thinking about kind of…

10:44.561 --> 10:45.604
Um…

10:45.687 --> 10:48.690
[country pop music playing on speakers]

10:54.821 --> 10:56.823
- [Shelby] Totally my fault.
- [Kris] Yeah, I'm starving.

10:56.907 --> 10:57.908
[friend] All right. Me too.

10:57.991 --> 11:00.035
Um, we were thinking about…
Well, let's get some oysters.

11:00.118 --> 11:01.286
- This is cute.
- Thank you.

11:01.370 --> 11:02.829
And I know you like shrimp cocktails,

11:02.913 --> 11:04.998
- so we could get a bit of everything.
- Yeah, shrimp is good.

11:05.082 --> 11:09.169
Um, I don't know,
we could all get soup if we want.

11:09.253 --> 11:10.379
I'll probably get a burger.

11:10.462 --> 11:11.463
Hello.

11:12.798 --> 11:14.132
Um…

11:15.008 --> 11:16.176
So I'm not sure if you heard,

11:16.260 --> 11:19.179
but I'm throwing a party
here tomorrow night.

11:19.263 --> 11:20.973
Do you mean the municipal event?

11:22.182 --> 11:25.978
Yeah, Kris, the city's sponsoring it,
but I'm the chair and it's my party,

11:26.061 --> 11:28.856
so you're more than welcome to come.

11:29.606 --> 11:31.942
But I'd RSVP
'cause space is pretty limited

11:32.025 --> 11:34.862
and we're expecting a lot of people.

11:34.945 --> 11:38.156
Everybody's going to Bill Rooney's
birthday at the Elks Lodge tomorrow.

11:41.493 --> 11:42.828
Oh, Bill's having a party?

11:44.121 --> 11:49.293
Um… Well, that's actually a relief 'cause,
what with all the tourists,

11:49.376 --> 11:52.462
I was worried that we'd have
to turn people away at the doors.

11:52.546 --> 11:54.673
[chuckles] Oh, I think you'll be okay.

11:57.551 --> 11:58.802
Enjoy your lunch.

12:00.387 --> 12:01.930
- Thanks.
- [Shelby] Yeah.

12:02.764 --> 12:04.099
[inhales deeply]

12:06.977 --> 12:10.230
- [Kris] No one is going to that.
- [group snickering]

12:11.064 --> 12:12.065
[Kris] Seriously.

12:12.149 --> 12:15.777
[unsettling, discordant music playing]

12:33.253 --> 12:35.255
[music continues]

12:41.720 --> 12:44.848
I mean, there were probably
800 songs on that list.

12:44.932 --> 12:48.101
It's like she wrote down every song
she's ever heard in her life.

12:48.185 --> 12:49.770
- And then she--
- [Rosemary clears throat]

13:00.405 --> 13:03.242
Where are we with RSVPs
for Sunset Cocktails?

13:03.325 --> 13:04.576
[stammers]

13:09.915 --> 13:11.166
Zero people.

13:12.417 --> 13:14.878
Why'd you even hand me this?
Just say no one's RSVP'd.

13:14.962 --> 13:15.963
[stammers]

13:17.589 --> 13:18.590
I didn't want to.

13:18.674 --> 13:19.675
Oh.

13:21.009 --> 13:24.805
The Elks Lodge isn't permitted to have
more than 30 nonmembers at a time.

13:25.681 --> 13:30.018
Call Glen. Tell him Bill Rooney's
big birthday tonight is canceled,

13:30.102 --> 13:31.979
unless he wants me
to unleash hell on their little club

13:32.062 --> 13:34.147
when their liquor license
is up for renewal.

13:44.449 --> 13:46.368
[unsettling, discordant music playing]

14:03.427 --> 14:04.845
[mouse clicks]

14:08.682 --> 14:09.766
[mouse clicks]

14:12.186 --> 14:13.353
[tapping on keyboard]

14:18.192 --> 14:21.820
[Bechir sighs] Okay, Loftis.
Let's waste my time.

14:23.405 --> 14:24.615
[sighs]

14:25.782 --> 14:28.994
Mayor called to see
if you found that old lady yet.

14:31.330 --> 14:33.957
Driscoll, do you think
I'm here for my own entertainment?

14:34.041 --> 14:36.960
I mean, it's not like I'm back here
watching, uh, Footloose.

14:37.920 --> 14:38.921
Copy that.

14:48.931 --> 14:49.932
[taps on keyboard]

14:57.314 --> 14:58.690
[taps on keyboard]

14:58.774 --> 15:00.984
[eerie music playing]

15:02.027 --> 15:03.278
[taps on keyboard]

15:04.863 --> 15:06.615
[ominous music playing]

15:06.698 --> 15:07.950
What the hell?

15:14.373 --> 15:16.375
[crickets chirping]

15:29.054 --> 15:31.056
[unsettling music playing]

15:35.477 --> 15:37.479
[chopping continues]

15:47.239 --> 15:48.615
Listen. I'm…

15:48.699 --> 15:50.117
[chopping stops]

15:50.200 --> 15:51.618
[chopping resumes]

15:51.702 --> 15:54.788
I'm a little worried
you're putting too much into this thing.

15:54.872 --> 15:55.873
I…

15:55.956 --> 15:58.917
I didn't even understand
half the stuff on that supply list.

15:59.001 --> 16:01.962
And might I suggest a different headpiece?

16:02.045 --> 16:04.173
Rosemary, I don't need
your negativity right now.

16:04.256 --> 16:05.424
Just be supportive.

16:06.341 --> 16:07.759
[chopping continues]

16:08.760 --> 16:10.929
[Rosemary] I can't do
anything right today.

16:14.099 --> 16:16.101
[breathing heavily]

16:17.603 --> 16:18.645
[taps on microphone]

16:18.729 --> 16:20.355
[mic feedback]

16:20.439 --> 16:21.690
[Dale] Check, check, one, two.

16:21.773 --> 16:23.901
Check, check, check, check one, two.

16:23.984 --> 16:26.028
Check, check, check one, two.

16:26.111 --> 16:29.364
- Check, check, check, check one, two.
- [inhales sharply]

16:29.448 --> 16:31.533
Check, check, check one, two.

16:31.617 --> 16:32.618
Check, check--

16:32.701 --> 16:35.954
It started 15 minutes ago.
Why are you still saying, "check"?

16:36.038 --> 16:38.248
It's a surprisingly complicated system.

16:38.332 --> 16:40.626
- This is death, Dale.
- Okay, I'm gonna try something--

16:40.709 --> 16:43.545
Hi there! Are you two visiting
from out of town?

16:43.629 --> 16:45.839
- Yeah.
- Great! We're just getting started.

16:45.923 --> 16:47.424
Okay, cool. [chuckles]

16:47.508 --> 16:50.552
- We'll circle back.
- No! Come, have a drink.

16:50.636 --> 16:55.390
Okay. So this is the dance floor,
if you wanna get your boogie on.

16:55.474 --> 16:57.267
Um, or not, you know. [chuckles]

16:57.351 --> 17:00.354
Um, have you met Dr. Calvin Morgan?

17:00.979 --> 17:02.773
I'm sure he'll have a great medical story.

17:02.856 --> 17:05.108
I'm off the clock tonight, Patricia.

17:05.192 --> 17:07.027
[Ruth] I've got a good one for you.

17:07.611 --> 17:08.945
It started in the foot.

17:09.029 --> 17:10.948
[huffs] Oh, my God. Damn it!

17:11.031 --> 17:12.241
What? What?

17:12.324 --> 17:15.285
They're sitting right at the entrance
and I was trying to dress the room,

17:15.368 --> 17:16.537
you know what I'm saying?

17:17.162 --> 17:18.579
[softly] I got it.

17:18.664 --> 17:21.333
- All right, fuggos, let's go.
- No, no, no, no.

17:21.415 --> 17:23.042
[Kurt] You're out of deviled eggs.

17:23.794 --> 17:26.630
Okay. I'll get those… get the, uh…

17:26.713 --> 17:28.966
[unsettling, discordant music playing]

17:37.432 --> 17:38.433
To who?

17:43.480 --> 17:45.899
- [line ringing]
- [inhales sharply, exhales deeply]

17:48.777 --> 17:51.113
Well, Tom, I don't know where you are,

17:51.196 --> 17:53.448
but I am at the event…

17:55.075 --> 17:56.577
that you said you would be at!

17:57.369 --> 17:59.037
[inhales deeply, exhales shakily]

18:02.749 --> 18:05.169
- Where are the good-looking people?
- I don't know.

18:05.252 --> 18:07.546
Did you see where
the good-looking people went?

18:07.629 --> 18:09.756
Has anyone seen the good-looking people?

18:09.840 --> 18:12.467
Oh, I see them.
They're at the top of the stairs.

18:12.551 --> 18:13.552
[snickering] Oh, my God.

18:13.635 --> 18:16.180
- [Rosemary] They are good-looking.
- [Ruth] Oh. Oh, yes. Gorgeous.

18:16.263 --> 18:17.472
- Yeah.
- [snickering continues]

18:17.556 --> 18:20.726
- ["This Is How We Do It" playing]
- Okay, come on!

18:20.809 --> 18:23.937
Whoo! Party! All right.

18:25.772 --> 18:28.108
[advertiser on speakers]
Affected by male-pattern baldness?

18:28.192 --> 18:30.068
Come see how we do it--

18:30.152 --> 18:32.362
- Why is there an ad?
- [guests snickering]

18:32.446 --> 18:33.447
I don't have premium.

18:33.530 --> 18:36.783
- Good night, Patricia.
- What? No, it's just… It's too early.

18:36.867 --> 18:39.203
[group whispering]

18:39.286 --> 18:41.580
[bachelorette party chattering]

18:41.663 --> 18:44.291
[cheering]

18:46.043 --> 18:48.754
Let's get these bachelorettes shots!

18:48.837 --> 18:50.839
[cheering]

18:50.923 --> 18:53.634
["Only You Know What I Like" playing]

18:59.932 --> 19:02.392
Crab cake? Crab cake?

19:03.519 --> 19:04.853
- Uh, crab cake?
- Oh.

19:06.146 --> 19:08.941
Mmm. This is delicious.

19:09.525 --> 19:11.193
- [chuckles]
- Is it your recipe?

19:11.276 --> 19:12.945
If I said yes, would you believe me?

19:13.654 --> 19:15.489
You shouldn't. [snickering]

19:15.572 --> 19:19.201
Uh, I'm gonna get some more crab cakes.

19:20.202 --> 19:23.872
[Kris] Seriously, what the fuck
is on her head? [chuckles]

19:23.956 --> 19:26.333
[group snickering]

19:26.416 --> 19:27.960
[inhales deeply]

19:29.253 --> 19:30.963
Why are you always so nasty to me?

19:31.797 --> 19:33.215
Oh, here we go.

19:33.882 --> 19:35.717
Look who gets to play victim again.

19:35.801 --> 19:38.637
You know what, Kris,
I don't even care if you believe me.

19:38.720 --> 19:42.099
He came to my house,
and I hid under the bed, and he--

19:42.182 --> 19:43.433
You hid under the bed?

19:44.434 --> 19:46.895
Oh, my God. I… I didn't know that.

19:47.980 --> 19:49.439
Guys, she hid under her bed.

19:50.983 --> 19:52.234
How clever.

19:52.317 --> 19:55.237
I can't believe none
of the other girls thought to hide.

19:55.904 --> 19:57.990
Oh, wait, they did.

19:58.073 --> 20:01.034
Samantha was stabbed
and then she hid in the dryer.

20:01.118 --> 20:04.454
Of course, he turned it on
and, well, she baked to death.

20:04.538 --> 20:09.918
And Jen… Jen hid under her covered pool,
but he was already waiting there for her.

20:10.460 --> 20:14.256
But you… You hid under a bed.

20:15.007 --> 20:16.550
That must be his kryptonite.

20:17.426 --> 20:19.428
- He can't look under beds.
- I…

20:19.511 --> 20:24.057
I don't know why he didn't find me,
but he was there and I--

20:24.141 --> 20:25.350
Just let it go!

20:26.268 --> 20:27.269
Let it go.

20:27.936 --> 20:30.939
My friends died.

20:31.648 --> 20:35.068
And you are just so,
so starved for attention

20:35.152 --> 20:36.987
that you had to make that about you.

20:47.206 --> 20:49.208
[tense, eerie music playing]

20:52.085 --> 20:54.087
[sobbing]

20:58.467 --> 20:59.468
[music stops]

20:59.551 --> 21:01.136
- [imitates yawning]
- I'm-I'm sorry,

21:01.220 --> 21:02.971
I thought this was the bathroom.

21:04.223 --> 21:06.475
[sobbing]

21:07.559 --> 21:10.187
[music resumes]

21:11.396 --> 21:12.564
[sniffles]

21:15.025 --> 21:16.443
[sniffles, exhales sharply]

21:19.321 --> 21:20.322
[gulps]

21:20.405 --> 21:22.824
[ominous music playing]

21:39.967 --> 21:40.968
[exhales]

21:43.887 --> 21:46.890
["Let's Dance" playing]

21:49.726 --> 21:51.144
Punch is served!

21:52.062 --> 21:54.064
[cheering]

22:26.722 --> 22:28.348
Come on, let's dance.

22:29.016 --> 22:30.475
Oh… [chuckles] …sorry.

22:31.560 --> 22:32.936
[yelps, chuckles]

22:39.526 --> 22:41.987
[partner, on radio]
This one in Hingham has a den.

22:42.571 --> 22:44.489
I could use it as a craft room.

22:45.282 --> 22:48.660
How about a craft beer room?
I've been thinking about brewing my own.

22:48.744 --> 22:50.746
Funny way of asking for a divorce.

22:50.829 --> 22:51.830
[laughs]

22:52.539 --> 22:53.916
Isn't your shift over?

22:55.918 --> 23:01.256
Uh, well, Loftis is convinced that, uh,

23:01.840 --> 23:04.051
there's some crazy old lady on the loose.

23:04.635 --> 23:07.304
Mm-hmm. Yeah, and she's waiting
for you to come home.

23:09.556 --> 23:10.641
I'm on my way.

23:11.934 --> 23:14.353
Oh, oh. Can you pick up
some mint chocolate chip?

23:15.521 --> 23:16.688
Already on it.

23:17.773 --> 23:20.234
[Driscoll] Got a noise complaint
at the Salty Whale.

23:22.653 --> 23:23.695
I don't care.

23:24.863 --> 23:27.032
It's Patricia's event.
Should I shut it down?

23:30.285 --> 23:31.370
Uh…

23:32.746 --> 23:35.958
Uh, no. No, I'll go myself.

23:40.838 --> 23:42.422
[engine starts]

23:42.506 --> 23:46.927
["The Rhythm of the Night" playing]

24:38.395 --> 24:40.355
[ominous music playing]

24:41.940 --> 24:42.941
[chuckles]

24:44.443 --> 24:46.528
[coughs] Oh! [chuckles]

24:47.362 --> 24:48.530
Sorry. [chuckles]

24:49.031 --> 24:51.783
Um, I'm a little nervous. [chuckles]

24:51.867 --> 24:53.410
- [chuckling]
- You've got this, baby.

24:53.493 --> 24:54.703
[chuckles]

24:56.038 --> 24:57.289
[inhales deeply]

24:58.040 --> 25:00.876
It means so much
that you're all here tonight.

25:00.959 --> 25:04.129
It's such a wonderful night for our town.

25:04.213 --> 25:06.298
Um… [clicks tongue]

25:06.381 --> 25:08.884
I'm kind of at a loss
for words honestly. [chuckles]

25:08.967 --> 25:11.386
- [crowd chuckles]
- Aw!

25:11.470 --> 25:15.057
[hopeful music playing]

25:18.519 --> 25:19.520
[sighs]

25:22.314 --> 25:26.527
"As I look around this room
at friends old and new…

25:28.779 --> 25:29.947
I feel grateful.

25:32.074 --> 25:35.661
For there is always time to change
the course of history.

25:40.415 --> 25:44.086
And tonight, tomorrow starts today."

25:47.589 --> 25:50.843
- To new beginnings! [laughs]
- [cheering, laughing]

25:52.469 --> 25:54.054
Cheers. [laughs]

25:54.137 --> 25:55.639
- [all cheering]
- Cheers!

25:57.683 --> 25:59.852
Let's go down to the cove for the bonfire.

25:59.935 --> 26:01.478
[crowd cheers]

26:01.562 --> 26:02.563
[Shelby] Let's go, Patricia.

26:02.646 --> 26:05.190
- Oh. [laughs]
- [guest] Yeah, Patricia!

26:05.274 --> 26:06.692
Yeah, I'll just get some more punch.

26:06.775 --> 26:08.944
- [guest 2] Yeah. Let's go!
- Come on. [chuckles]

26:18.745 --> 26:19.746
[clears throat]

26:20.873 --> 26:22.875
[sighs] What's your problem?

26:24.710 --> 26:27.796
I didn't understand
one word of that speech.

26:28.797 --> 26:34.386
I know that you asked me to be supportive,
but I have my qualms.

26:34.469 --> 26:35.679
That's all I'm gonna say.

26:35.762 --> 26:36.763
[door opens]

26:37.347 --> 26:39.766
[Patricia] Bechir! Finally off duty?

26:39.850 --> 26:42.186
Uh, no. No, I, uh…

26:42.769 --> 26:44.563
I had a noise complaint.

26:44.646 --> 26:47.858
Oh. [inhales sharply]
Sorry, I guess people are having fun.

26:47.941 --> 26:49.276
[chuckling]

26:53.447 --> 26:57.201
[unsettling music playing]

27:06.335 --> 27:07.419
[whispers] Patricia.

27:09.546 --> 27:10.631
What, uh…

27:13.926 --> 27:15.552
What the fuck are you doing?

27:22.976 --> 27:25.229
[sinister music playing]

27:35.239 --> 27:36.740
[whimpers] Oh, my God.

27:36.823 --> 27:39.076
[pants] Oh, my God. [breathes shakily]

27:39.159 --> 27:40.786
[Rosemary] We tried to tell her.

27:40.869 --> 27:43.080
[Patricia] You had your qualms?

27:43.163 --> 27:46.208
- Why didn't you say anything?
- You told me to be supportive!

27:46.291 --> 27:48.377
[breathing heavily]

27:49.378 --> 27:51.171
What have I… What have I done?

27:51.255 --> 27:53.882
[tense music playing]

28:21.994 --> 28:24.997
[ominous music playing]

28:27.124 --> 28:29.835
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

28:30.627 --> 28:32.629
Oh, no. [panting]

28:33.463 --> 28:34.464
Oh, my God.

28:35.924 --> 28:38.468
[breathing shakily]

28:38.552 --> 28:39.970
Oh, no. No.

28:45.475 --> 28:47.060
[breathes heavily]

28:47.144 --> 28:48.395
Oh, my God.

28:48.478 --> 28:52.065
[tense, ominous music playing]

28:54.651 --> 28:57.362
- [footsteps running]
- [Patricia breathing heavily]

29:02.201 --> 29:04.703
[all groaning]

29:09.708 --> 29:12.878
You guys! What are you doing?

29:12.961 --> 29:14.796
Stop! Stop!

29:15.464 --> 29:16.757
Stop!

29:16.840 --> 29:19.301
- Get back! [grunting]
- [groaning resumes]

29:19.384 --> 29:21.887
[grunts] Get back! Whoa, whoa.

29:21.970 --> 29:23.972
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

29:24.723 --> 29:27.893
Whoa! Why is no one listening?

29:27.976 --> 29:31.730
I told you it's for… [exclaims]

29:31.813 --> 29:33.273
What the hell is going on?

29:33.357 --> 29:34.816
- Just…
- [groaning continues]

29:34.900 --> 29:36.902
…get them out! Save them!

29:36.985 --> 29:39.238
[stammers] Come on.
[stammers] Everybody, stay here!

29:39.321 --> 29:42.115
Stay here! Hey! Excuse me, hey!
Get outta here!

29:42.199 --> 29:43.617
Oh, shit. Come here.

29:44.493 --> 29:46.161
Hey! You!

29:46.745 --> 29:48.330
[grunts] Hey, come here!

29:49.998 --> 29:52.251
Out of the water! Out of the water!

29:52.334 --> 29:54.086
Everybody, get outta here! Go!

29:54.169 --> 29:55.295
[panting]

29:57.130 --> 29:59.466
Rescue station one,
this is Sheriff Clemmons.

29:59.550 --> 30:02.594
All available fire and rescue
to Patricia's Cocktails.

30:02.678 --> 30:04.179
I don't know what the fuck is going on!

30:04.263 --> 30:07.015
Hey! No, ma'am. Back this way!

30:11.645 --> 30:12.688
[screams]

30:13.480 --> 30:15.357
[Patricia panting] What?

30:15.440 --> 30:17.276
[straining]

30:20.195 --> 30:22.614
No, this way. Get back here!

30:23.907 --> 30:26.535
[breathing heavily] That'll kill 'em.

30:32.082 --> 30:34.459
- [groaning]
- [voices echoing]

30:47.639 --> 30:51.310
[voice groaning, howling]

30:55.105 --> 30:58.192
[wood cracking]

31:03.947 --> 31:05.157
[Bechir] Come here! Come here.

31:05.741 --> 31:07.367
Out of the water. Stop!

31:07.451 --> 31:08.744
[music stops]

31:08.827 --> 31:10.871
[all mumbling indistinctly]

31:13.123 --> 31:14.958
What the fuck happened?

31:15.584 --> 31:18.420
[breathing heavily, sighs]

31:19.671 --> 31:20.797
Oh, my God.

31:22.257 --> 31:23.717
We were drugged.

31:25.719 --> 31:27.387
It was that goddamn punch.

31:28.889 --> 31:31.183
It was her goddamn punch!

31:31.767 --> 31:33.101
She drugged us!

31:42.861 --> 31:44.363
[tires screech]

31:44.446 --> 31:45.447
[Tom] Patricia?

31:48.867 --> 31:49.868
You okay?

31:51.662 --> 31:52.913
No.

31:55.874 --> 31:57.709
Something bad happened at the party.

31:59.795 --> 32:00.796
It went wrong.

32:02.130 --> 32:04.842
Ah, you can file that under
"deal with it the fuck later."

32:04.925 --> 32:05.926
[Tom] Why don't…

32:07.427 --> 32:10.222
Why don't you just get in with us?

32:11.390 --> 32:12.599
We might need your help.

32:13.725 --> 32:16.562
[gentle music playing]

32:16.645 --> 32:17.646
Come on.

32:23.360 --> 32:24.403
[tires squeal]

32:32.452 --> 32:34.997
- [Patricia] What was wrong with him?
- [Tom] I don't know.

32:35.080 --> 32:36.665
He just sounded scared.

32:37.249 --> 32:38.959
[Wyck] Because he knows something.

32:39.042 --> 32:42.045
[ominous music playing]

32:47.509 --> 32:48.510
Bryce!

33:00.230 --> 33:01.398
[Tom shushes]

33:29.218 --> 33:30.219
[sighs]

33:30.928 --> 33:33.472
[chilling music playing]

33:40.062 --> 33:43.065
[sinister music playing]
